Harbor: ID2D1Effect::SetInput accepts NULL (#93).

It called AddRef on the new input before looking at it. Clearing an input is ordinary use: Excel does it
several hundred times while starting, and crashed on the first.

Test: WindowsTests/d2d/run.sh.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/effect.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/effect.c
@@ -2927,7 +2927,8 @@
     if (index >= effect->input_count)
         return;
 
-    ID2D1Image_AddRef(input);
+    if (input)
+        ID2D1Image_AddRef(input);
     if (effect->inputs[index])
         ID2D1Image_Release(effect->inputs[index]);
     effect->inputs[index] = input;
